/github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/mand_oled.py"&gt;mand_oled&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Pico W Temperature</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico3/</link><pubDate>Tue, 17 Jan 2023 12:29:22 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico3/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Have been tinkering with temperature measurement using the Raspberry Pi Pico.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;First with the internal temperature sensor and then using a TMP36 temperature sensor externally.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I wrote two classes to access these and return the reading.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/library/internal_temp.py"&gt;Internal Temperature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/library/tmp36.py"&gt;External Temperature&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is an example using the two sensors together &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/temps.py"&gt;temps.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You will need to upload the two classes to the Pico first in a &lt;code&gt;library&lt;/code&gt; sub-directory.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is how you would wire it up on a breadboard &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/circuits/tmp36.fzz"&gt;tmp36.fzz&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Rasberry Pi Pico W OLED</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico2/</link><pubDate>Tue, 10 Jan 2023 13:38:21 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico2/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Some components arrived from AliExpress recently so been able to play with an I2C OLED display with my Pico W.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Hello World Test&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="wp-caption alignnone"&gt;&#10; &lt;a data-flickr-embed="true" data-header="true" data-footer="false"&#10; data-context="false"&#10; href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/52611812353"&#10; title="Hello World"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/52611812353_596b54ceff_c.jpg" width="800" alt="Hello World" /&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;script async src="//embedr.flickr.com/assets/client-code.js" charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text"&gt;Hello World Test&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Code of this is here &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/i2c_scan.py"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/i2c_scan.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;And also used here to display the IP address after connected to the wifi &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/wifi_oled.py"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w/blob/main/wifi_oled.py&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Next thing I&amp;rsquo;ve been playing with is internal and external temperature sensors, I will post about that soon.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Raspberry Pi Pico W</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Jan 2023 13:31:23 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pico/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Just before Christmas I got a Raspberry Pi Pico W to have a play with.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Looking forward to using MicroPython to do some LED flashing and other things.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Started a repo on Github for it &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/pico_w"&gt;Pico W Repo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Day 169 Light holiday reading</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-169-light-holiday-reading/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Sep 2013 14:26:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/day-169-light-holiday-reading/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; the only link in this post is now broken. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml'&gt;&lt;img style='max-width:586px;' src='http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7289/9732431638_e1d213ac15_b.jpg'/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div&gt;New Arduino book :) http://flic.kr/p/fQ2fRu, September 12, 2013 at 04:11PM&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>123D Circuits</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/123d-circuits/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Sep 2013 14:13:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/123d-circuits/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Been trying out &lt;a href="http://123d.circuits.io/" target="_blank"&gt;123D Circuits&lt;/a&gt; an GITHUB style online circuit designer and simulator.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe frameborder="0" height="448" marginheight="0" marginwidth="0" scrolling="no" src="http://123d.circuits.io/circuits/28975/embed" width="725"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Dusting off the iron</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dusting-off-iron/</link><pubDate>Mon, 03 Dec 2012 21:44:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dusting-off-iron/</guid><description>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;My first attempt at soldering after around eight years away from the soldering iron.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEikMpfbHZuWO0H9p8JmE27n2M8JfJuTsZTH0sumqZqEMDWL_ckxRjT0eWg4-5Q8xfLhwO21L8MabTciR944pom0l7A5B0btpJ9BLw6QkaZqfHl3e8w9XauVuWxOFLN0HyERvct7mUdZvRY/' /&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;img src='https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEidVlVDjmYLj4gwrtdmWSrbjyvQzVCQ3k4GL_ClyaSh2WbIzy2dpZvSX1MCsX2L1q6NEACN3H1iU8GE2htRFOeEZ4hgeq-0NjtfwlWtRCVcAAVt1pFlLJx3U0OTKCArqoDzmEqr1Mzde4Q/' /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Counting up to 1023</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</link><pubDate>Sun, 25 Nov 2012 22:03:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/counting-up-to-1023/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Decided in the end to wire up all 10 LEDS in the LED bar graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Using the sketch below get the results shown in the video.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/1TVgph8aZE4/0.jpg" height="266" width="320"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/1TVgph8aZE4?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; numLed = 10;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledpins[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,5,4};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; i=0;i&amp;lt;numLed;i++){&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(ledpins[i], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;(250);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Arduino Binary second counter</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Nov 2012 14:46:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/arduino-binary-second-counter/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Next step with my Arduino is to set up a binary second counter.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Basic using the LED Bar Graph or six single LEDs to count seconds in binary&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s1600/six+leds_bb.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="290" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjNmgs8Izk2utl30ZAVCskDyYVZ2wMyj97vYfOIO-uxLJk1cOgJ_ZaY-_LZmbyjDATFZWzCzKZQVxI7P1Y1obG7oL9eIb0x5no0MF79yfG4KTp3ruXU9Xn-ZY-ZUMVihaNaLlNvoxhBcW8/s320/six+leds_bb.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;/*&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;Binary&amp;nbsp;Second&amp;nbsp;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;Created&amp;nbsp;Alastair&amp;nbsp;Montgomery&amp;nbsp;22/11/2012&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;*/&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledPins[] = {&#10;  7,8,9,10,11,12};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mask[] = {&#10;  1,2,4,8,16,32};&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; ledCount = 6;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; thisPin =0; thisPin &amp;lt; ledCount; thisPin++) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(ledPins[thisPin], &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sanity Checking my new Arduino Uno Board</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Nov 2012 22:13:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/sanity-checking-my-new-arduino-uno-board/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Quick sanity check of my new Arduino board using a LED Bar Graph.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;object width="320" height="266" class="BLOGGER-youtube-video" classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="http://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=6,0,40,0" data-thumbnail-src="https://ytimg.googleusercontent.com/vi/L7ri5PBrsQU/0.jpg"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" /&gt;&lt;param name="bgcolor" value="#FFFFFF" /&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true" /&gt;&lt;embed width="320" height="266" src="https://www.youtube.com/v/L7ri5PBrsQU?version=3&amp;f=user_uploads&amp;c=google-webdrive-0&amp;app=youtube_gdata" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Here is the sketch I will be using.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led1 = 8;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; led2 = 9;&#10;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; counter = 0;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() { &lt;br&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #7e7e7e;"&gt;// initialize the digital pin as an output.&lt;/span&gt;&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;pinMode&lt;/span&gt;(led2, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/span&gt;);&lt;br&gt;&#10;}&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;() {&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (counter &amp;amp; 1) {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;HIGH&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&#10;  &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; {&#10;    &lt;span style="color: #cc6600;"&gt;digitalWrite&lt;/span&gt;(led1, &lt;span style="color: #006699;"&gt;LOW&lt;/span&gt;);&#10;  }&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>